{"id":"fact-example-001","type":"code_quirk","fact":"Example: The UserService caches results for 5 minutes, so updates may not appear immediately in queries.","recommendation":"Use cache invalidation after writes, or query with { fresh: true } option.","confidence":"medium","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"discovered during debugging","date":"2026-01-15"}],"tags":["caching","user-service"],"affectedFiles":["src/lib/services/user.service.ts"],"affectedServices":["UserService"],"createdAt":"2026-01-15T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-15T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id": "fact-frontend-harness-lifecycle-001", "type": "code_quirk", "fact": "Frontend AI-Harness/tmux sessions are spawned in createTab (Frontend/API.hs), not by the dispatcher tab factory: createHarnessTab calls the injected _fe_startHarness seam, persists the returned TmuxConfig into _sm_kind, and registers the handle in the shared _fe_harnesses map (== _env_harnesses, the same harnessRef IORef wired in CLI/Commands.hs). handleSend then routes SkHarness sessions to _hh_send/_hh_receive instead of the LLM provider.", "recommendation": "To add/modify frontend harness behaviour, edit createHarnessTab + handleSend in Frontend/API.hs and the _fe_startHarness impl in CLI/Commands.hs (delegates to startHarnessByName). The dispatcher's Tab.Harness.mkTabHarness only ADOPTS an already-running harness.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "epic pureclaw-99a / PR fix-frontend-harness-tmux-spawn", "date": "2026-06-01"}], "tags": ["frontend", "harness", "tmux", "sessions"], "affectedFiles": ["src/PureClaw/Frontend/API.hs", "src/PureClaw/CLI/Commands.hs"], "affectedServices": ["FrontendEnv"], "createdAt": "2026-06-01T00:00:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-06-01T00:00:00Z", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "fact-frontend-harness-restart-reconnect-001", "type": "code_quirk", "fact": "Restart reconnect for frontend harness sessions works because discoverHarnesses (boot) re-keys the shared harness map by tmux window name, which equals harnessKey = canonical<>\"-\"<>show windowIdx, which is persisted as TmuxConfig._tc_window in the session's _sm_kind. handleSend recomputes the key via harnessKeyFromKind and finds the rediscovered handle.", "recommendation": "Keep the three in sync: the renameWindow target, the _env_harnesses map key, and the persisted _tc_window must all be the same harnessKey string.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "epic pureclaw-99a", "date": "2026-06-01"}], "tags": ["frontend", "harness", "tmux", "restart"], "affectedFiles": ["src/PureClaw/Frontend/API.hs", "src/PureClaw/Agent/SlashCommands.hs"], "affectedServices": ["FrontendEnv"], "createdAt": "2026-06-01T00:00:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-06-01T00:00:00Z", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "fact-handrolled-test-main-registration-001", "type": "code_quirk", "fact": "The Haskell test suite uses a hand-rolled test/Main.hs (NOT hspec-discover). A new spec module is invisible unless registered in BOTH test/Main.hs (import qualified + a describe ... .spec line) AND the pureclaw.cabal test stanza other-modules.", "recommendation": "When adding a spec module, register it in test/Main.hs AND pureclaw.cabal other-modules, or it silently won't run.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "epic pureclaw-3oy (Harness Registry Phase 1)", "date": "2026-06-01"}], "tags": ["testing", "haskell", "cabal", "build"], "affectedFiles": ["test/Main.hs", "pureclaw.cabal"], "affectedServices": [], "createdAt": "2026-06-02T03:03:45.298808+00:00", "updatedAt": "2026-06-02T03:03:45.298808+00:00", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
